    "plan": "Callboard row 2026-11-30 (storyhowto, story-howto), the earliest planned row on 2026-11-25; look collage",
    "project": "ppvqmbzuqvzpiuqaiqfy",
    "sql": "select m.id, m.character_name, m.estimated_duration_seconds, m.overdone_score, p.title, p.author, p.copyright_status from monologues m join plays p on p.id=m.play_id where p.title ilike '%little shop%'",
    "checked": "2026-11-25: play 4595 Little Shop of Horrors (Howard Ashman, copyrighted): 46167 Seymour 48s, 46168 Seymour 60s, 46169 Audrey 50s, 46170 Orin Scrivello 58s, overdone 0. In the Ghost Light app 'Little Shop of Horrors' returns Seymour 0:48, Seymour 1 min, Audrey 0:50 first, 30 monologues",
    "changed_from_plan": "the row's search ('a monologue for a musical audition, under a minute') and two other described asks return film cards first (The Greatest Showman, tick, tick... BOOM!, Rent), not the new stage pieces, so the film types the show's name. Not swapped to i36: the hook and the new library pieces stay true. Copyrighted: show, character, writer and length only, the speech text is blurred on every screen (and Tonight's speech on the search screen)",
